---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const methods = [
  {
    name: "fuzz",
    body: "40+ cargo-fuzz harnesses across 17+ crates, one per untrusted-parse surface, asserting Err-not-panic. Input size and resource amplification capped; CI smoke-runs every harness on a short budget, deep runs manual.",
  },
  {
    name: "loom",
    body: "Every Tier A concurrency primitive carries loom models — minimum 2 interleaving scenarios per invariant, proven non-vacuous (a seeded race must be caught). breaker's models explore every bounded interleaving of concurrent failure recording and trip/success races.",
  },
  {
    name: "Kani",
    body: "Bounded model checking of the breaker state machine: state never leaves {Closed, Open, HalfOpen}, and an Open circuit implies ≥ threshold recorded failures — for all nondeterministic op sequences. Each harness verifies in <60 s.",
  },
  {
    name: "DST",
    body: "Deterministic simulation seed sweeps: property generators with every counterexample seed persisted to proptest-regressions/ and re-run in CI, plus sustained-delivery sweeps (actor-kit: 500k cumulative messages across 10 rounds, 10/10 green after the 0.1.1 drain-stall fix).",
  },
  {
    name: "Quint",
    body: "The CRDT merge semantics are specified in Quint; the model checker reports no violations of convergence properties, cross-checked against the proptest-verified RGA implementation in crdts-kit.",
  },
  {
    name: "mutation",
    body: "cargo-mutants weekly on every kit (Tier A profile, --all-features). Survivors are triaged as MISSING TEST / EQUIVALENT / UNVIABLE with written rationale. Gates graduate to blocking (--fail-under) after 4 stable weeks.",
  },
];

const mutationBaselines = [
  { crate: "barbican", mutants: 10, killed: 7, score: "100%" },
  { crate: "chronoshift (clock)", mutants: 49, killed: 45, score: "100%" },
  { crate: "healthkit", mutants: 19, killed: 15, score: "100%" },
  { crate: "salting", mutants: 60, killed: 51, score: "100% of tested (51/51)" },
  { crate: "breaker", mutants: 89, killed: 58, score: "98.3%" },
  { crate: "money (decimal-money)", mutants: 124, killed: 107, score: "97.3%" },
  { crate: "tokenkit", mutants: 32, killed: 25, score: "96.2%" },
  { crate: "validkit", mutants: 291, killed: 178, score: "95.7%" },
  { crate: "otelkit", mutants: 16, killed: 12, score: "92.3%" },
];

const slos = [
  {
    crate: "breaker",
    number: "37 ns, 0-alloc",
    body: "CircuitBreaker::call allowed path (closed circuit): 37 ns mean — SLO <50 ns. Rejected path (open): 46 ns — SLO <60 ns. Both paths ~0 allocations across 10,000 calls (counting-alloc verified). CI gate is deterministic instruction counts via iai-callgrind; criterion stays as the human-readable trend.",
  },
  {
    crate: "actor-kit",
    number: "1.3 µs/msg",
    body: "Uncontended dispatch ≈1.3 µs/msg with 4 workers (~0.76 M msg/s). Backpressured delivery ≤15 µs/msg at 1 worker, ≤5 µs at 4. Spawn ≤1 ms SLO (measured ~580 µs, allocation-bound). Steal contention sustains 1.32 M msg/s at 8 producers.",
  },
  {
    crate: "ecosystem",
    number: "56/56 repos",
    body: "llvm-cov audit ran every Rust kit repo (2026-09-05) — thresholds A ≥90 / B ≥80 / C ≥70, hard gate flips 2026-10. Regression policy: CI fails on >20% P99 bench regression; alert at >2× mean on named hot-path benches.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Verification — WyattAu Kit Ecosystem"
  description="What's verified how across the WyattAu kits: fuzz harnesses, loom models, Kani verdicts, DST seed sweeps, Quint no-violations, mutation scores 92–100%, and measured SLOs like breaker at 37 ns / 0-alloc."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Verification Story</p>
    <h1>Verified, not vibes</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Six verification methods run continuously across the ecosystem. Every
      claim below has a number, a date, and a harness you can re-run — the
      Show-HN version of our engineering standards.
    </p>
    <div class="badges">
      {methods.map((m) => <span class="badge accent">{m.name}</span>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The methods</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      {
        methods.map((m) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mono" style="color: var(--accent);">{m.name}</h3>
            <p>{m.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Mutation scores (cargo-mutants 27.1.0, 2026-09)</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Crate</th>
            <th scope="col">Mutants</th>
            <th scope="col">Killed</th>
            <th scope="col">Viable-kill score</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            mutationBaselines.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <td><span class="crate-name">{row.crate}</span></td>
                <td><span class="ver">{row.mutants}</span></td>
                <td><span class="ver">{row.killed}</span></td>
                <td>{row.score}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote">
      Unresolved survivors are equivalent-only so far — each recorded with a
      behavioral rationale in the crate's
      <span class="mono">mutants-equivalent.txt</span>. Full baselines and
      triage lessons in
      <a href="https://github.com/WyattAu/engineering-standards/blob/main/MUTATION.md">MUTATION.md</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Measured SLOs</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      {
        slos.map((slo) => (
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <h3 class="mono" style="color: var(--accent);">{slo.crate}</h3>
              <span class="badge accent">{slo.number}</span>
            </div>
            <p>{slo.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="footnote">
      Hardware for the quoted numbers: Intel Core i5-9400F @ 2.90 GHz, 6 cores,
      Linux x86_64, measured 2026-09 with criterion; P50 = criterion mean.
      Per-crate numbers in each repo's
      <span class="mono">PERF-SLO.md</span> (e.g.
      <a href="https://github.com/WyattAu/breaker/blob/main/PERF-SLO.md">breaker</a>,
      <a href="https://github.com/WyattAu/actor-kit/blob/main/PERF-SLO.md">actor-kit</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Model-checking verdicts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Kani (breaker):</strong> verified — for every bounded
        nondeterministic success/failure sequence, the state machine stays in
        its documented state space, and an Open circuit always has ≥
        <span class="mono">failure_rate_threshold</span> recorded failures.
        Frozen-clock stub documented in the harness; each harness verifies in
        &lt;60 s.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Loom (breaker):</strong> verified — concurrent failure
        recording never loses an update (circuit trips exactly once), and a
        <span class="mono">trip()</span>/<span class="mono">record_success()</span>
        race ends Open with exactly one transition, across every bounded
        interleaving.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Quint (crdts-kit):</strong> no violations — merge semantics
        model-checked against convergence properties; implementation
        independently proptest-verified.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>DST (actor-kit):</strong> 10/10 green — sustained delivery of
        500k cumulative messages across 10 consecutive rounds after the 0.1.0
        drain-stall fix, with the regression test pinned in CI.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Honest ledger</h2>
    <p>
      Not everything is green, and we publish that too: the 2026-09 coverage
      audit put 33 of 56 repos at or above threshold — the hard gate flips
      2026-10, and the gap list with per-crate test estimates is public.
      Mutation baselines are non-blocking until each crate's score is stable
      for 4 consecutive weeks. cargo-vet supply-chain audits are rolling out
      to Tier A, non-blocking until the exemption backlog is burned down.
    </p>
    <p class="footnote">
      Sources:
      <a href="https://github.com/WyattAu/engineering-standards/blob/main/COVERAGE.md">COVERAGE.md</a>
      ·
      <a href="https://github.com/WyattAu/engineering-standards/blob/main/MUTATION.md">MUTATION.md</a>
      ·
      <a href="https://github.com/WyattAu/engineering-standards/blob/main/REPRODUCIBILITY.md">REPRODUCIBILITY.md</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
